---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { skanpayDefinitions } from "../content/site";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="SkanPay - Checkout Value Platform"
  description="SkanPay helps participating wallets, merchants, and payment partners apply eligible value before the final balance is paid."
  activePath="/qr-payments/"
>
  <section class="tech-hero">
    <div class="tech-hero-inner">
      <div class="tech-hero-copy motion-item">
        <p class="eyebrow">SkanPay</p>
        <h1>Apply eligible value before the final payment.</h1>
        <p>
          SkanPay is the broader product direction behind BeamCash: a patent-pending checkout value platform for participating wallets, merchants, payment partners, and promotion programs.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="request-object motion-item" aria-label="SkanPay checkout outcome snapshot">
        <div><span>Customer</span><strong>Presents eligible wallet or offer value</strong></div>
        <div><span>Merchant</span><strong>Applies value at checkout</strong></div>
        <div><span>Payment</span><strong>Final balance is paid</strong></div>
        <div><span>Result</span><strong>Confirmation shows what happened</strong></div>
        <div><span>Partner</span><strong>Starts with one measured pilot</strong></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="definition-section">
    <div class="definition-inner">
      <div class="tech-section-heading motion-item">
        <p class="eyebrow">Definition</p>
        <h2>The product is the checkout outcome, not the QR code.</h2>
        <p>The customer should not need to think about separate offer redemption and payment steps. The public promise is simple: apply eligible value, pay the final balance, and confirm the result.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="definition-lines" aria-label="What SkanPay is and is not">
        {skanpayDefinitions.map((group) => (
          <article class="motion-item">
            <h3>{group.label}</h3>
            <ul>
              {group.items.map((item) => (
                <li>{item}</li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="state-machine">
    <div class="state-machine-inner">
      <div class="tech-section-heading motion-item">
        <p class="eyebrow">Checkout flow</p>
        <h2>What a participating checkout should make possible.</h2>
        <p>The flow should be easy to repeat: present value, apply value, pay the balance, confirm the result.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="state-rail" aria-label="SkanPay checkout flow">
        <article class="motion-item">
          <span>Present</span>
          <strong>Customer presents eligible value</strong>
          <p>The value may come from a participating wallet, coupon, voucher, gift card, or loyalty program.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="motion-item">
          <span>Apply</span>
          <strong>Checkout applies what qualifies</strong>
          <p>The merchant keeps control of the invoice and determines what can apply to the purchase.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="motion-item">
          <span>Pay</span>
          <strong>Final balance is paid</strong>
          <p>The checkout continues through the supported payment path after the eligible value is handled.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="motion-item">
          <span>Confirm</span>
          <strong>Results are confirmed</strong>
          <p>The right participants can receive confirmation of what was redeemed, charged, and completed.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="protocol-split">
    <div class="protocol-split-inner">
      <div class="protocol-copy motion-item">
        <p class="eyebrow">For partners</p>
        <h2>Start with one narrow pilot.</h2>
        <p>
          The master business direction is not a universal launch on day one. It is one value source, one merchant environment, one payment path, and one redemption problem with a clear success measure.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="boundary-map motion-item" aria-label="Gateway and partner responsibilities">
        <div>
          <span>Wallet or offer owner</span>
          <strong>Make value usable</strong>
          <p>Help customers use an existing account, coupon, voucher, gift card, or loyalty benefit in a new participating checkout.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>Merchant or platform</span>
          <strong>Keep checkout control</strong>
          <p>Keep invoice logic, eligibility, and merchant operations inside the systems that already own them.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>Payment partner</span>
          <strong>Reduce one-off work</strong>
          <p>Support a repeatable checkout pattern instead of a custom connection for every wallet, merchant, and offer source.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="integration-runway">
    <div class="integration-runway-inner">
      <div class="tech-section-heading motion-item">
        <p class="eyebrow">Pilot scope</p>
        <h2>What we would define before testing.</h2>
        <p>The useful first conversation is practical: what value should apply, where checkout happens, who confirms the outcome, and how success is measured.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="runway-list">
        <li class="motion-item"><span>01</span><strong>Participating wallet or value source</strong></li>
        <li class="motion-item"><span>02</span><strong>Merchant checkout environment</strong></li>
        <li class="motion-item"><span>03</span><strong>Coupon, voucher, gift card, or loyalty rule</strong></li>
        <li class="motion-item"><span>04</span><strong>Final payment and confirmation path</strong></li>
        <li class="motion-item"><span>05</span><strong>Success measure and data boundaries</strong></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
